<mjml>
  <mj-head>
    <mj-attributes>
      <mj-all font-family="'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif" />
      <mj-text font-size="15px" color="#5A5A50" line-height="1.6" />
    </mj-attributes>
  </mj-head>
  <mj-body background-color="#F4F2EC">

    <mj-section background-color="#2D4A2A" padding="0">
      <mj-column padding="0">
        <mj-text padding="5px 0" font-size="0" line-height="0">&nbsp;</mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <mj-section background-color="#ffffff" padding="32px 40px 0">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text align="center" padding="0">
          <span style="display:inline-block;width:36px;height:36px;border-radius:9px;background:#2D4A2A;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;font-style:italic;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#C8F060;text-align:center;line-height:36px;">C</span>
          &nbsp;
          <span style="font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:700;color:#1A1A14;letter-spacing:-0.02em;vertical-align:middle;">Claro<em style="font-style:italic;">Bill</em></span>
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- Intro -->
    <mj-section background-color="#ffffff" padding="28px 40px 8px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text font-size="13px" color="#9A9A8E" letter-spacing="0.06em" padding-bottom="12px">
          THIS WEEK FROM CLAROBILL
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text font-family="Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif" font-size="24px" font-weight="700" color="#1A1A14" line-height="1.3" letter-spacing="-0.02em" padding-bottom="12px">
          You sent the letter. Here is what happens in the next 30 days.
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text padding-bottom="0">
          Most people send a dispute letter and then wait. Passively. That is the single biggest mistake in the dispute process.
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- Divider -->
    <mj-section background-color="#ffffff" padding="20px 40px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-divider border-color="#E2DDD4" border-width="1px" />
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- Article -->
    <mj-section background-color="#ffffff" padding="0 40px 8px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text font-size="11px" font-weight="700" color="#2D4A2A" letter-spacing="0.07em" padding-bottom="10px">
          GUIDE
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text font-family="Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif" font-size="20px" font-weight="700" color="#1A1A14" line-height="1.3" letter-spacing="-0.02em" padding-bottom="12px">
          What Happens After You Send a Medical Bill Dispute Letter
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text padding-bottom="16px">
          Hospital billing departments run disputes through an internal review that typically takes 2 to 4 weeks. You will not hear much during that window. The silence does not mean the dispute is going well or badly. It means a coder has not gotten to it yet.
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text padding-bottom="16px">
          What you do right now matters more than the letter itself:
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text font-size="14px" padding-bottom="10px">
          <span style="color:#2D4A2A;font-weight:600;">Pay the part you are not disputing.</span> Do not withhold the full bill. Pay what you agree is correct and isolate the contested amount in writing. Withholding everything looks like non-payment, not a dispute.
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text font-size="14px" padding-bottom="10px">
          <span style="color:#2D4A2A;font-weight:600;">Document your proof of delivery.</span> Certified mail tracking number, email read receipt, fax confirmation. If the hospital later claims they never received your letter, you need proof.
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text font-size="14px" padding-bottom="10px">
          <span style="color:#2D4A2A;font-weight:600;">Set a reminder for day 30.</span> If you have not heard back, call. Ask for the name of the person handling your dispute and a written status update by a specific date. Every follow-up needs a deadline.
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text font-size="14px" padding-bottom="20px">
          <span style="color:#2D4A2A;font-weight:600;">Know your escalation paths.</span> A denial from the billing department is not a final answer. Your insurer's appeals process, your state insurance commissioner, and the hospital's own patient advocate are all options most people never use because they do not know they exist.
        </mj-text>
        <mj-button background-color="#2D4A2A" color="#ffffff" border-radius="999px" font-size="15px" font-weight="700" letter-spacing="0.01em" href="https://www.clarobill.com/learn/what-happens-after-you-dispute-a-medical-bill?utm_source=loops&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=after-dispute-letter" inner-padding="14px 32px">
          Read the full guide
        </mj-button>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- Quick Hits -->
    <mj-section background-color="#ffffff" padding="28px 40px 8px">
      <mj-column background-color="#F4F2EC" border-radius="12px" padding="20px 24px">
        <mj-text font-size="12px" font-weight="700" color="#2D4A2A" letter-spacing="0.06em" padding-bottom="12px">
          QUICK HITS
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text font-size="13px" padding-bottom="10px">
          <span style="color:#2D4A2A;font-weight:600;">There are three responses.</span> Full resolution, partial resolution, or denial. Each one has a different next step. A denial is a prompt to escalate, not a reason to stop.
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text font-size="13px" padding-bottom="10px">
          <span style="color:#2D4A2A;font-weight:600;">If the bill goes to collections during your dispute,</span> notify the collections agency in writing immediately and include a copy of your original dispute letter. Federal law requires them to pause collection activity on a disputed debt.
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text font-size="13px" padding-bottom="10px">
          <span style="color:#2D4A2A;font-weight:600;">A partial resolution does not close the matter.</span> You can continue disputing remaining charges in a second letter. Acknowledge the adjustment and restate your dispute on what is left.
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text font-size="13px" padding-bottom="0">
          <span style="color:#2D4A2A;font-weight:600;">Most disputes fail because patients stop following up,</span> not because the hospital was right. Set the reminder. Make the call on day 30.
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- Sign off -->
    <mj-section background-color="#ffffff" padding="24px 40px 36px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text padding-bottom="0">
          Thanks for trusting ClaroBill to help you navigate your medical bills. We are here every step of the way.
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <mj-section background-color="#ffffff" border-top="1px solid #E2DDD4" padding="20px 40px 28px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text font-size="12px" color="#9A9A8E">
          &copy; 2026 ClaroBill &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;
          <a href="https://www.clarobill.com/legal/privacy" style="color:#9A9A8E;">Privacy</a> &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;
          <a href="https://www.clarobill.com/legal/terms" style="color:#9A9A8E;">Terms</a> &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;
          <a href="mailto:support@clarobill.com" style="color:#9A9A8E;">support@clarobill.com</a> &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;
          <a href="{unsubscribe_link}" style="color:#9A9A8E;">Unsubscribe</a>
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

  </mj-body>
</mjml>
